        "operation": {
          "permanent": true,
          "notes": "Monitoring is organised on a monthly and seasonal basis in approximately 20 and 62 lakes and other lentic aquatic ecosystems, respectively. The landscape is monitored by remote sensing and other sensors. For some parameters such as temperature, conductivity, pH and others, the frequency is hourly. \r\n",
          "siteVisitInterval": 12
        },
        "notes": "The National Park has a large structure with rooms for meetings, rooms for researchers and students, laboratories and accommodation for researchers. In terms of equipment, there is a large structure with multi-probes for temperature, pH and other parameters, permanent probes for temperature and other parameters, equipment for laboratory analyses and others. This structure of facilities provides the conditions for carrying out biological and abiotic analyses on Santa Cruz Island, the main basis for the long-term site. However, it is important to emphasise that all the inhabited islands (Santa Cruz, San Cristobal, Isabela and Genovesa) have all the structures for sampling, such as helicopters, boats, cars for transport, etc.",
