            "notes": "The Freshwater Galapagos Programme Coordination will define a document to ensure that the research programme and the subprojects envisaged in this programme commit to making the subproject data available in a common platform or database. Once signed, each document will be attached to the programme and forwarded to the Galapagos National Park. A copy will be archived with the other documents of this programme. This unique database will facilitate the writing of articles, and papers jointly with different approaches such as multi-taxonomic, ecological redundancy, trophic interactions and modelling of climatic, landscape use, hydrological, physical, chemical and biotic markers, among others. All collaborators will be included as co-authors. The first and last author will be decided in a formal meeting. This perspective will be used in all Galapagos research programmes, such as marine, terrestrial and fauna."
